# An allowlist: the images install only these trees, and Dockerfile.submission's
# image is handed to teams. Everything else in the checkout stays out -- organizer-only
# packs (private/, mounted at run time), weights, outputs and repo history.
*
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!capx
!docker
!env_configs
!taskpacks

# Inside those trees: build and run leftovers (docker/setup-behavior.sh puts a venv
# and ~55 GB of assets under b1k) and the key files docker/run.sh and the LLM
# proxies read.
**/.git
**/.venv*
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/outputs
capx/third_party/b1k/datasets
**/api_keys.yaml
**/hf_token
**/.env
**/.openaikey
**/.openrouterkey
**/.nvinferencekeys
**/.webui_secret_key
